WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.882
Asking questions.

2
00:00:02.132 --> 00:00:04.778
Question words usually
come first in the sentence.

3
00:00:04.928 --> 00:00:09.024
Almost all of them are fixed. So
learn each one with its last vowel.

4
00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.838
Part one. Question isms.
This is the table to learn.

5
00:00:13.088 --> 00:00:17.388
These question words are isms. Each
one asks for one kind of answer.

6
00:00:17.738 --> 00:00:21.223
Each row has the word, its
meaning, a question, and an answer.

7
00:00:21.373 --> 00:00:22.094
‫مَنْ‬

8
00:00:22.294 --> 00:00:23.968
Who. It asks for a person.

9
00:00:24.118 --> 00:00:26.267
‫مَنْ فِي الْغُرْفَةِ؟‬

10
00:00:26.517 --> 00:00:27.561
Who is in the room?

11
00:00:27.711 --> 00:00:28.787
‫مُحَمَّدٌ‬

12
00:00:29.037 --> 00:00:31.184
Muhammad. The answer is a person.

13
00:00:31.534 --> 00:00:32.981
Row two has two words.

14
00:00:33.131 --> 00:00:33.846
‫مَا‬

15
00:00:33.996 --> 00:00:34.785
‫مَاذَا‬

16
00:00:34.985 --> 00:00:38.330
Both words have the same meaning,
what. They ask for a thing.

17
00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:39.489
‫مَا هَذَا؟‬

18
00:00:39.739 --> 00:00:40.665
What is this?

19
00:00:40.815 --> 00:00:42.274
‫هَذَا كِتَابٌ‬

20
00:00:42.524 --> 00:00:44.748
This is a book. The answer is a thing.

21
00:00:45.098 --> 00:00:45.808
‫مَتَى‬

22
00:00:46.008 --> 00:00:47.609
When. It asks for a time.

23
00:00:47.759 --> 00:00:50.146
‫مَتَى خَرَجَ الْمُدَرِّسُ؟‬

24
00:00:50.396 --> 00:00:51.719
When did the teacher go out?

25
00:00:51.869 --> 00:00:53.570
‫بَعْدَ الظُّهْرِ‬

26
00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:55.860
After noon. The answer is a time.

27
00:00:56.210 --> 00:00:57.058
‫أَيْنَ‬

28
00:00:57.258 --> 00:00:58.954
Where. It asks for a place.

29
00:00:59.104 --> 00:01:00.957
‫أَيْنَ الْكِتَابُ؟‬

30
00:01:01.207 --> 00:01:02.174
Where is the book?

31
00:01:02.324 --> 00:01:03.903
‫عَلَى الْمَكْتَبِ‬

32
00:01:04.153 --> 00:01:06.396
On the desk. The answer is a place.

33
00:01:06.746 --> 00:01:07.499
‫كَيْفَ‬

34
00:01:07.699 --> 00:01:09.421
How. It asks for a state.

35
00:01:09.571 --> 00:01:11.072
‫كَيْفَ حَالُكَ؟‬

36
00:01:11.322 --> 00:01:12.271
How are you?

37
00:01:12.421 --> 00:01:13.564
‫بِخَيْرٍ‬

38
00:01:13.814 --> 00:01:15.640
Fine. The answer is a state.

39
00:01:15.990 --> 00:01:16.707
‫كَمْ‬

40
00:01:16.907 --> 00:01:19.531
How many, or how much.
It asks for a number.

41
00:01:19.681 --> 00:01:22.554
‫كَمْ طَالِبًا فِي الْفَصْلِ؟‬

42
00:01:22.804 --> 00:01:24.887
How many students are in the classroom?

43
00:01:25.037 --> 00:01:26.378
The answer is a number.

44
00:01:26.728 --> 00:01:27.765
‫لِمَاذَا‬

45
00:01:27.965 --> 00:01:29.809
Why. It asks for a reason.

46
00:01:29.959 --> 00:01:33.889
‫لِمَاذَا ذَهَبْتَ إِلَى الْمَسْجِدِ؟‬

47
00:01:34.139 --> 00:01:35.507
Why did you go to the mosque?

48
00:01:35.657 --> 00:01:37.069
‫لِلصَّلَاةِ‬

49
00:01:37.319 --> 00:01:39.730
For the prayer. The answer is a reason.

50
00:01:41.967 --> 00:01:43.978
Now learn the last vowel of each word.

51
00:01:44.228 --> 00:01:45.701
These two end in sukūn.

52
00:01:45.851 --> 00:01:46.572
‫مَنْ‬

53
00:01:46.672 --> 00:01:47.389
‫كَمْ‬

54
00:01:47.639 --> 00:01:48.988
These two end in fatha.

55
00:01:49.138 --> 00:01:49.986
‫أَيْنَ‬

56
00:01:50.086 --> 00:01:50.839
‫كَيْفَ‬

57
00:01:51.089 --> 00:01:52.640
These four end in a long ā.

58
00:01:52.790 --> 00:01:53.505
‫مَا‬

59
00:01:53.605 --> 00:01:54.394
‫مَاذَا‬

60
00:01:54.494 --> 00:01:55.204
‫مَتَى‬

61
00:01:55.304 --> 00:01:56.341
‫لِمَاذَا‬

62
00:01:56.591 --> 00:01:59.280
These endings never change.
The words are fixed.

63
00:01:59.730 --> 00:02:02.410
Three tips. First, there
are two words for what.

64
00:02:02.560 --> 00:02:03.275
‫مَا‬

65
00:02:03.425 --> 00:02:04.214
‫مَاذَا‬

66
00:02:04.464 --> 00:02:07.668
The short one is usual before
a noun. What is your name?

67
00:02:07.818 --> 00:02:09.089
‫مَا اسْمُكَ؟‬

68
00:02:09.339 --> 00:02:12.566
The long one is usual before
a verb. What did you write?

69
00:02:12.716 --> 00:02:14.098
‫مَاذَا كَتَبْتَ؟‬

70
00:02:14.548 --> 00:02:16.126
Second, the word for how many.

71
00:02:16.276 --> 00:02:16.993
‫كَمْ‬

72
00:02:17.193 --> 00:02:20.359
After it comes one noun with
tanween fatha. How many books?

73
00:02:20.509 --> 00:02:21.781
‫كَمْ كِتَابًا؟‬

74
00:02:22.031 --> 00:02:25.025
The noun is singular, even
though the meaning is plural.

75
00:02:25.475 --> 00:02:26.757
Third, the word for why.

76
00:02:26.907 --> 00:02:27.944
‫لِمَاذَا‬

77
00:02:28.144 --> 00:02:31.199
It is made of two parts.
The first part means for.

78
00:02:31.349 --> 00:02:31.841
‫لِ‬

79
00:02:32.041 --> 00:02:33.697
The second is the word for what.

80
00:02:33.847 --> 00:02:34.636
‫مَاذَا‬

81
00:02:34.836 --> 00:02:36.328
Together they mean: for what?

82
00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:40.295
Part two. Question ḥarfs.

83
00:02:40.445 --> 00:02:41.162
‫هَلْ‬

84
00:02:41.312 --> 00:02:41.758
‫أَ‬

85
00:02:42.008 --> 00:02:45.274
These two turn a normal sentence
into a yes or no question.

86
00:02:45.424 --> 00:02:47.232
The answer starts with yes or no.

87
00:02:47.382 --> 00:02:48.199
‫نَعَمْ‬

88
00:02:48.349 --> 00:02:49.088
‫لَا‬

89
00:02:49.438 --> 00:02:51.673
Is this a house? Yes, this is a house.

90
00:02:51.823 --> 00:02:53.540
‫هَلْ هَذَا بَيْتٌ؟‬

91
00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.579
‫نَعَمْ، هَذَا بَيْتٌ‬

92
00:02:55.929 --> 00:03:00.546
Without the question ḥarf, this is a
normal sentence. With it, it is a question.

93
00:03:00.896 --> 00:03:02.986
Is this a pen? No, this is a key.

94
00:03:03.136 --> 00:03:04.755
‫أَهَذَا قَلَمٌ؟‬

95
00:03:05.005 --> 00:03:07.085
‫لَا، هَذَا مِفْتَاحٌ‬

96
00:03:07.435 --> 00:03:10.710
Here the question ḥarf is the
short one at the very start.

97
00:03:10.710 --> 00:03:12.856
It is written joined to the next word.

98
00:03:13.006 --> 00:03:14.761
This one is from the Madinah book.

99
00:03:15.111 --> 00:03:17.043
Did Ali go to the principal? Yes.

100
00:03:17.193 --> 00:03:20.968
‫أَذَهَبَ عَلِيٌّ إِلَى الْمُدِيرِ؟‬

101
00:03:21.218 --> 00:03:22.035
‫نَعَمْ‬

102
00:03:22.385 --> 00:03:26.068
It is the same small ḥarf. This
time it is joined to a verb.

103
00:03:26.518 --> 00:03:28.558
So there are two kinds of question word.

104
00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.048
A question ism has a job in the sentence.

105
00:03:31.198 --> 00:03:34.102
It asks for a person, a
thing, a place or a time.

106
00:03:34.452 --> 00:03:36.084
A question ḥarf has no job.

107
00:03:36.234 --> 00:03:38.232
It only makes a yes or no question.

108
00:03:38.682 --> 00:03:41.601
Never answer a where, who or
when question with yes or no.

109
00:03:41.751 --> 00:03:44.558
Only the two question ḥarfs
take a yes or no answer.

110
00:03:44.708 --> 00:03:45.425
‫هَلْ‬

111
00:03:45.575 --> 00:03:46.021
‫أَ‬

112
00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:50.251
Part three. With a preposition.

113
00:03:50.501 --> 00:03:52.872
A preposition can come
before a question word.

114
00:03:53.022 --> 00:03:56.578
The question word is still fixed.
It is in the place of jarr.

115
00:03:57.028 --> 00:03:59.234
Where are you from? I am from India.

116
00:03:59.384 --> 00:04:01.203
‫مِنْ أَيْنَ أَنْتَ؟‬

117
00:04:01.453 --> 00:04:03.567
‫أَنَا مِنَ الْهِنْدِ‬

118
00:04:03.917 --> 00:04:07.366
Here the word for where comes
after the preposition meaning from.

119
00:04:07.516 --> 00:04:08.913
‫مِنْ أَيْنَ‬

120
00:04:09.163 --> 00:04:12.294
It still ends in fatha. It
is in the place of jarr.

121
00:04:12.744 --> 00:04:15.132
Where did Khalid go to? To the market.

122
00:04:15.282 --> 00:04:18.214
‫إِلَى أَيْنَ ذَهَبَ خَالِدٌ؟‬

123
00:04:18.464 --> 00:04:20.288
‫إِلَى السُّوقِ‬

124
00:04:20.638 --> 00:04:24.444
Again a preposition comes first.
The question word does not change.

125
00:04:24.894 --> 00:04:26.199
How much is this book?

126
00:04:26.349 --> 00:04:28.684
‫بِكَمْ هَذَا الْكِتَابُ؟‬

127
00:04:29.034 --> 00:04:33.099
The word for how much has a small
preposition joined to its front.

128
00:04:33.099 --> 00:04:36.794
That preposition means for.
Together they ask: for how much?

129
00:04:36.944 --> 00:04:37.774
‫بِكَمْ‬

130
00:04:38.024 --> 00:04:40.113
The question word still ends in sukūn.

131
00:04:40.563 --> 00:04:41.718
Whose pen is this?

132
00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.658
‫قَلَمُ مَنْ هَذَا؟‬

133
00:04:44.008 --> 00:04:47.827
Here the word for who comes after
the word for pen. It is the owner.

134
00:04:47.977 --> 00:04:48.698
‫مَنْ‬

135
00:04:48.948 --> 00:04:52.793
It keeps its sukūn. As the owner,
it is in the place of jarr.

136
00:04:53.343 --> 00:04:53.709
A tip.

137
00:04:53.709 --> 00:04:58.650
Without a preposition before it, a question
word has its own job in the sentence.

138
00:04:58.900 --> 00:04:59.944
Who is in the room?

139
00:05:00.094 --> 00:05:02.243
‫مَنْ فِي الْغُرْفَةِ؟‬

140
00:05:02.593 --> 00:05:06.194
Here the word for who is the
Topic. It is in the place of rafʿ.

141
00:05:08.434 --> 00:05:11.123
Part four. A question
word that is not fixed.

142
00:05:11.273 --> 00:05:12.140
‫أَيٌّ‬

143
00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:13.770
It is the word for which.

144
00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.512
This word takes endings.

145
00:05:15.662 --> 00:05:18.333
It is a question ism. But it is flexible.

146
00:05:18.483 --> 00:05:22.904
It is the exception. Every other
question word in this lesson is fixed.

147
00:05:23.154 --> 00:05:24.954
Its ending changes with its job.

148
00:05:25.104 --> 00:05:27.405
And the noun after it
is jarr, as its owner.

149
00:05:27.855 --> 00:05:29.023
Which book is this?

150
00:05:29.173 --> 00:05:31.271
‫أَيُّ كِتَابٍ هَذَا؟‬

151
00:05:31.621 --> 00:05:34.718
Here the word for which is
in rafʿ. It ends in damma.

152
00:05:34.868 --> 00:05:35.648
‫أَيُّ‬

153
00:05:35.898 --> 00:05:40.573
The noun after it is its owner. So the
noun is jarr, with kasra and tanween.

154
00:05:40.723 --> 00:05:41.627
‫كِتَابٍ‬

155
00:05:41.877 --> 00:05:45.360
Because the noun is its owner,
the question word has no tanween.

156
00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:47.103
Which book did you read?

157
00:05:47.253 --> 00:05:49.595
‫أَيَّ كِتَابٍ قَرَأْتَ؟‬

158
00:05:49.945 --> 00:05:52.893
Here it is the object. So
it is naṣb, with fatha.

159
00:05:53.043 --> 00:05:53.765
‫أَيَّ‬

160
00:05:54.215 --> 00:05:55.770
In which room is the principal?

161
00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:59.338
‫فِي أَيِّ غُرْفَةٍ الْمُدِيرُ؟‬

162
00:05:59.688 --> 00:06:03.879
Here it comes after a preposition.
That preposition means in.

163
00:06:03.879 --> 00:06:05.665
So it is jarr, with kasra.

164
00:06:05.815 --> 00:06:06.662
‫أَيِّ‬

165
00:06:07.012 --> 00:06:11.200
Rafʿ, naṣb and jarr. Three endings.
That is what flexible means.

166
00:06:13.434 --> 00:06:15.742
Part five. Which word for which answer?

167
00:06:15.992 --> 00:06:19.289
Look at the kind of answer.
Then choose the question word.

168
00:06:19.639 --> 00:06:20.998
The answer is a person.

169
00:06:21.148 --> 00:06:21.869
‫مَنْ‬

170
00:06:22.119 --> 00:06:22.837
A thing.

171
00:06:22.987 --> 00:06:23.702
‫مَا‬

172
00:06:23.802 --> 00:06:24.591
‫مَاذَا‬

173
00:06:24.841 --> 00:06:25.631
A time.

174
00:06:25.781 --> 00:06:26.491
‫مَتَى‬

175
00:06:26.741 --> 00:06:27.572
A place.

176
00:06:27.722 --> 00:06:28.570
‫أَيْنَ‬

177
00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:30.067
‫مِنْ أَيْنَ‬

178
00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:31.591
‫إِلَى أَيْنَ‬

179
00:06:31.841 --> 00:06:32.616
A state.

180
00:06:32.766 --> 00:06:33.519
‫كَيْفَ‬

181
00:06:33.769 --> 00:06:35.085
A number or a price.

182
00:06:35.235 --> 00:06:35.952
‫كَمْ‬

183
00:06:36.052 --> 00:06:36.882
‫بِكَمْ‬

184
00:06:37.132 --> 00:06:37.897
A reason.

185
00:06:38.047 --> 00:06:39.084
‫لِمَاذَا‬

186
00:06:39.334 --> 00:06:40.273
One of a group.

187
00:06:40.423 --> 00:06:41.290
‫أَيٌّ‬

188
00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.502
Yes or no.

189
00:06:42.652 --> 00:06:43.369
‫هَلْ‬

190
00:06:43.469 --> 00:06:43.915
‫أَ‬

191
00:06:44.365 --> 00:06:45.217
In short.

192
00:06:45.467 --> 00:06:49.529
These question isms ask who, what,
when, where, how, how many and why.

193
00:06:49.529 --> 00:06:50.863
All of these are fixed.

194
00:06:51.213 --> 00:06:52.877
The question ḥarfs are these two.

195
00:06:53.027 --> 00:06:53.744
‫هَلْ‬

196
00:06:53.894 --> 00:06:54.340
‫أَ‬

197
00:06:54.540 --> 00:06:55.939
Answer them with yes or no.

198
00:06:56.289 --> 00:06:59.727
After a preposition, the question
word is in the place of jarr.

199
00:06:59.877 --> 00:07:01.274
‫مِنْ أَيْنَ‬

200
00:07:01.424 --> 00:07:02.254
‫بِكَمْ‬

201
00:07:02.604 --> 00:07:07.386
One question ism is not fixed. It is
the word for which. Its ending changes.

202
00:07:07.536 --> 00:07:08.316
‫أَيُّ‬

203
00:07:08.466 --> 00:07:09.188
‫أَيَّ‬

204
00:07:09.338 --> 00:07:10.185
‫أَيِّ‬

205
00:07:10.735 --> 00:07:12.019
Now it is your turn.

206
00:07:12.169 --> 00:07:15.250
Open the Practice tab and
work through the six cards.

207
00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.753
Then do the Homework tab.
